{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the fat that covers the innards</b> — this is the membrane over the paunch, which is called tila. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 29:13). In my opinion, \"the fat that covers the innards\" is the membrane, but when Scripture says \"all the fat that covers the innards,\" it alludes to the two fats that are there: to this membrane-fat, and to the coarse fat that is upon the innards, as is stated in the section of Vayikra (Leviticus 3:3), \"and the fat that covers the innards, and all the fat that is upon the innards.\" Now there are two fats upon the innards: sometimes Scripture mentions both of them, and sometimes it includes them as one with the word \"all\" (kol). Here, in \"all the fat that covers the innards,\" it also includes the fat that is upon the innards. And there, in the account of this very offering, it says, \"and he took all the fat that is upon the innards, and the appendage of the liver\" (Leviticus 8:16) — it included them in \"all the fat that is upon the innards.\" And further below in this passage (Exodus 29:22) it says, \"and you shall take from the ram the fat, and the fat tail, and the fat that covers the innards\" — and the first one mentioned, unspecified, is the fat that is upon the innards."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:18:00.609082571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}